#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "4dac81da-f15c-55ff-9630-7349a3e03e57" :question/math-academy-id "e-8273" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t),$ given by\n\n$$\np_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad\n\tp_2(t)=-t+t^2.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/3274a690fa59f7d7368fcbe54004eab244c9845e20bf03ffce1e9fa25bbaf4bc.png)" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/170acd827e8b97471869159c5d9af88b0e4324b25ca1b42ec652011ece6a5174.png)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =4\\cdot (3+2t)+(-3)\\cdot (-t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12+8t+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =12+11t-3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/id #uuid "aac4b559-b26b-57b0-8701-b3235969cd2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-8274" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/8a495251bb5d61eab1568624a6e1c213ccee49ec98fc8d5ff5c17fc841d027bf.png)\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ B_1, B_2 \\},$ calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/342997674c65cf5c4d14f0b2a7df2649bf99a8b0c003be93efa983f317faa7a1.png)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/ebd814bcb627ef3b9208bc0960bdaf48b9448396ed7e95d18d8c4abbf1169244.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=18 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-9 & =-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/dfc845ca1739c329e5636726466c76efee7eba19df4adc0909110506f894e72d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/id #uuid "f0fc412f-8276-5876-a509-4f2173396e72" :question/math-academy-id "e-8275" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\np_1(t)=5+t^2, \\quad\np_2(t)=3t-2t^2, \\quad\nq(t)=5-3t+3t^2.\n$$\n\nIf $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\},$ find $[q(t)]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(5+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(3t-2{t}^{2}) & =5-3t+3{t}^{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =5-3t+3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/195a50f130cc40c4a725066035f2da3ef25b725df96601e53f70716bd82b4f4a.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1.$ Therefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/9f23f71e833d7a7f81f511e1dfb72861ed753cb514de43d6cabfeb3c6b65fadb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "034d28dc-bddb-546b-b2a9-ca856946ff50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367432} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2d02ba-13a5-554a-9a5b-33138abff037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367433} {:answer/id #uuid "c615bbe7-5fa8-5c95-b74e-1fcb5157e024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367434} {:answer/id #uuid "da8c6082-9fc3-54ae-adf3-5181d9e294da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367435} {:answer/id #uuid "511021be-4fc1-5e5d-af0d-ee33b5168075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "034d28dc-bddb-546b-b2a9-ca856946ff50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367432} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d4b7fe2-441e-5524-90b9-0a9d8224bd7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6e0ce47-91dc-5e23-9eed-7afbcab835c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-106731" :question/problem "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B={{A}_{1},{A}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Span}{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1405f7d0-0c63-57d7-917e-bdcd478c70a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1+3{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367439} {:answer/id #uuid "f5aee792-0b83-5755-ada4-b58520de2b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+3{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367440} {:answer/id #uuid "40dad6c3-5ef4-5182-94bb-4e75088301d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367441} {:answer/id #uuid "c4570e4d-6dbd-5fb6-98b3-49558a9bb987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+7{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367442} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4ab561-ecca-57bb-8995-41648db1a16f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5aee792-0b83-5755-ada4-b58520de2b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+3{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367440} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6e5277b-f16d-59d2-ac9b-3a19a2327087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36c572db-161a-5a7b-ac35-d9a1bb392d6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106734" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}+{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+3{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =3\\cdot (2{t}^{2}+{t}^{3})+(-2)\\cdot (1+3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3}-2-6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-2+3{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02e7ecbb-8dda-5f74-95b0-670832ecbc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367446} {:answer/id #uuid "80660fc1-aced-5ad6-a49b-9aace7a3c793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367447} {:answer/id #uuid "3508ff3e-9a54-59c3-9029-4361f334ca00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367448} {:answer/id #uuid "61ac3570-5917-5024-b31f-df37e093b893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367449} {:answer/id #uuid "8f79dba4-92fa-553b-9133-d70ce03a3b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3508ff3e-9a54-59c3-9029-4361f334ca00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367448} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ec78ba-6cad-530a-9ab8-2c7a76809f7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16cc7fa0-2969-55cf-bb22-3a09b8235ac1" :question/math-academy-id "q-106738" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1+t+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =(-1)\\cdot (1+t+{t}^{2})+1\\cdot (1+t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-1-t-{t}^{2}+1+t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6c25450-143c-5989-b394-4c41a0954d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367453} {:answer/id #uuid "17628429-f69b-5236-9a21-11d3d0af5fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367454} {:answer/id #uuid "64fea624-acea-5cf4-b16d-0568f284b3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367455} {:answer/id #uuid "57c69f71-b8cb-5391-a29a-6dd0743209c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367456} {:answer/id #uuid "06a0f92a-05aa-5af5-902c-cc55ff38c8fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57c69f71-b8cb-5391-a29a-6dd0743209c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367456} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e007509-0bcf-592e-8589-2e45781774fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44ae9122-cee2-505f-a379-1662f2833f82" :question/math-academy-id "q-106754" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=20 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}=14 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 2 & =4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =8 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+2=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d407ee49-d375-5f07-96f7-3edff2a9b14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367460} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f09e20-8e48-5d9b-a50e-db968a8a1b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367461} {:answer/id #uuid "dde077ac-17fc-5257-b315-7fc1f1136f27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367462} {:answer/id #uuid "fc6db49c-f6cf-534f-9256-3ea85e849f3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367463} {:answer/id #uuid "2f2a6cca-1263-57ba-84d1-617ceb3fedbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8f09e20-8e48-5d9b-a50e-db968a8a1b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367461} :answer-field/id #uuid "3942f42e-f4aa-51bc-84fa-59c082b9c472" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d81b7258-84b1-569c-b6cf-ebc3733c7061" :question/math-academy-id "q-106781" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=6+2t.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(1-t+2{t}^{2}) & =6+2t \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =6+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$  Substituting this into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-2)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+(-2)=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "565fe992-55ff-572d-97b8-0d0cc7886a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367467} {:answer/id #uuid "81fad37a-ee5c-5e43-8625-45c1aa60de68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367468} {:answer/id #uuid "a3238e4d-f030-5358-b30c-66daee1c05f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367469} {:answer/id #uuid "1cdabdc3-6961-5383-9407-c467c5323a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367470} {:answer/id #uuid "0e29e7ba-7442-5d81-922e-828ba309aa4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81fad37a-ee5c-5e43-8625-45c1aa60de68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367468} :answer-field/id #uuid "4844ffc2-4da2-50c1-9190-04c1f8c9fc20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d88e3460-3c54-5531-89ee-fa4d53f324a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-106835" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}-2t+4,\\,{p}_{3}(t)={t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2,\\,\\,q(t)=2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({t}^{2}+t)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}-2t+4)+{x}_{3}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2) & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3} \\\\ (4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})t+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+{x}_{3}{t}^{3} & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4{x}_{2}-2\\cdot 1=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{1}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805a501b-a4fc-52a1-ac9f-33f7defa1351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165032} {:answer/id #uuid "e0858ade-2f58-56e3-8513-a3ba860887e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165033} {:answer/id #uuid "4afd8b98-e2ec-5e30-9eec-ac7582d8358b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165034} {:answer/id #uuid "4daedf73-e868-57d9-bff6-36c1fefb6a68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165035} {:answer/id #uuid "794e960d-3da4-5a66-93db-bbe39e9cd982" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "794e960d-3da4-5a66-93db-bbe39e9cd982" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165036} :answer-field/id #uuid "37bf8c30-b623-5449-8953-54b7ba172303" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df2010a4-a092-5afc-8c2a-1f95c6801456" :question/math-academy-id "q-36587" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} & 5{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{5}{4}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9690ca95-8d29-51c9-81db-4f75333330b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-5{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367474} {:answer/id #uuid "7bcc4325-f74b-5d8d-9f55-120442c27d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+4t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367475} {:answer/id #uuid "ab03593a-6334-5fee-8805-ae0f8d9e5b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367476} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc34621-52a6-5a6f-8c36-a1d3f8d0aaa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1-3t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367477} {:answer/id #uuid "91948abf-3c11-5964-af8e-c5fa4762fb6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-6{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab03593a-6334-5fee-8805-ae0f8d9e5b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367476} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7f991e1-2ea2-5c15-afc5-850c9276fa1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1319f607-fb08-5e4e-be32-36db233745ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-95003" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =1\\cdot (1-t+2{t}^{2})+3\\cdot (t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =1-t+2{t}^{2}+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2t-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b8f8032-e7de-59d0-8719-290cfa2369f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=3+2t+4{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367481} {:answer/id #uuid "898b0c7e-1bf5-5194-aee7-290bfa3e7a42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=3+t-2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367482} {:answer/id #uuid "92cbd4da-fdf1-50b0-9a79-0c638c1c2188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=6-2t+4{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367483} {:answer/id #uuid "a3ee60d5-90a2-54a8-b4e4-ba61903b71df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=6+2t-4{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367484} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8132f3-ea8a-5039-9fd7-b7bd506a8155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=6+t-2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3ee60d5-90a2-54a8-b4e4-ba61903b71df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=6+2t-4{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367484} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb0df23-cf61-50cf-a80d-c08cbdf12f8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84116a53-1342-5c6b-abeb-dda206837ef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95004" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t+{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=3-t-3{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =2\\cdot (2t+{t}^{3})+2\\cdot (3-t-3{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =4t+2{t}^{3}+6-2t-6{t}^{3} \\\\  & =6+2t-4{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fce6f491-9599-5367-aac9-715e94e4ea00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367488} {:answer/id #uuid "123a4976-8481-52fe-b3d0-b3027426bbf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367489} {:answer/id #uuid "aab392c5-9efe-5e63-b461-eca271523402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367490} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf79ca7-0f57-55c0-8882-f595d83222ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367491} {:answer/id #uuid "5708ea06-b04b-5638-a054-a56fe0c20711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcf79ca7-0f57-55c0-8882-f595d83222ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367491} :answer-field/id #uuid "dab64fb8-3555-5c2f-8161-57e09097b214" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84ea530c-a658-5939-9d7a-dcc4269fa091" :question/math-academy-id "q-95016" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} & -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}{x}_{2}=\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6\\cdot 1 & =-2 \\\\ 4{x}_{1} & =-8 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-2+1=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ee55576-9bba-592f-a54a-bf90901ec82a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367495} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce0956e-19a7-56e6-91eb-768d935e33ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367496} {:answer/id #uuid "befce8bc-d889-5fdb-b67c-29beff1198ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367497} {:answer/id #uuid "0529de1a-e2f7-523f-b1f3-efaea7141ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367498} {:answer/id #uuid "faded25f-b002-5c83-accb-c26c50c30a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ce0956e-19a7-56e6-91eb-768d935e33ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367496} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a95c201-0b8b-55b7-b96d-5085de88ffe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afea1de7-9432-5f54-8eea-c94a31190309" :question/math-academy-id "q-95019" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} & -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 9{x}_{2}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5\\cdot 1 & =4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f9c0363-5960-510b-bb27-0c46b7229f37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367502} {:answer/id #uuid "739cd2a1-5a1e-53dc-8acb-f2b06faf2244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367503} {:answer/id #uuid "05f3ae63-922a-5860-b37b-e32c286bfc69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367504} {:answer/id #uuid "4e791db8-f35b-58c5-8e02-3d2b6c2d0081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367505} {:answer/id #uuid "acd0504f-f5b9-5d55-9e5b-172b1742dc12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739cd2a1-5a1e-53dc-8acb-f2b06faf2244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367503} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8560350-b85b-576d-a9b0-536bd49e1a1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13bb45a0-733a-5979-8561-2d8d7531fe0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95021" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & -3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 9{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -6{x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "432c972d-a34d-5ad7-87ed-923cbb136266" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367509} {:answer/id #uuid "70c9b3a0-4b4a-571c-a226-40141eee0344" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367510} {:answer/id #uuid "a42cacb6-31ee-505b-943b-1e4537622faf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367511} {:answer/id #uuid "d46cb614-c679-53d3-905c-80b50fd55a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367512} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc9f2c4-da0a-53ff-86e9-2a375d1dba52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dc9f2c4-da0a-53ff-86e9-2a375d1dba52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367513} :answer-field/id #uuid "8301840e-7f8b-5d52-a6b5-5b10da290368" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fcdc7d3c-69b8-5cef-bcd7-6562e616e04a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95023" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+t)+{x}_{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & =2+3t+4{t}^{2} \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{1}t-{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}=3 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-4)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0345acee-6e41-54ee-b14b-a61bb205ee9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367516} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd9a18a-7609-5002-bc53-17908ef0e765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367517} {:answer/id #uuid "0a54e637-064a-5845-abe5-8dc53ac277ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367518} {:answer/id #uuid "8022aefe-4682-52e0-8235-99a02c080319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367519} {:answer/id #uuid "e6bd710b-e32d-5fa6-8592-a94ea9592a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a54e637-064a-5845-abe5-8dc53ac277ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367518} :answer-field/id #uuid "b32bd0f3-66e4-5dac-b2f1-148d081ef694" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1676a3ff-fcb1-5054-9d57-868a55967c3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95030" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}+t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+3t-6,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2},\\,\\,q(t)=-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{t}^{2}+t-2)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}+3t-6)+{x}_{3}(-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}{t}^{3}+(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})t+(-2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-5{x}_{2}+3\\cdot 1=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "374d3563-41a5-51c6-93e5-c4d7358a0ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367523} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f96750-b2db-5034-80a4-9f92c926c377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367524} {:answer/id #uuid "42b3f908-dcc2-5231-b3fc-3e645f86168d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367525} {:answer/id #uuid "24266f26-8cbd-51f3-98ed-e7061225ccb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367526} {:answer/id #uuid "05888a38-fbdc-5671-882f-ffed16f41343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5f96750-b2db-5034-80a4-9f92c926c377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367524} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ba7f75f-81d0-5cbb-ba23-0dc7c282f102" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "062748fc-307b-5d8e-a117-e78a8a5bc2f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95031" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=-{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2{t}^{2}+4,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=3{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-3t+3,\\,\\,q(t)=-1.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+t)+{x}_{2}(2{t}^{2}+4)+{x}_{3}(3{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-3t+3) & =-1 \\\\ (-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{3}+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+({x}_{1}-3{x}_{3})t+(4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}↔{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+2\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{3}=1.$"}]}
